Upstream-PR:     https://github.com/iiab/iiab/pull/4505
Upstream-Status: open (carried until it ships in the pinned iiab commit)
Applies-to:      roles/forgejo/* (new role); roles/0-init/tasks/{validate_*,disallow_*} (forgejo asserts); roles/6-generic-apps/tasks/main.yml (role include); roles/proot_services (pdsm forgejo service + mariadb responsiveness wrapper); roles/matomo/defaults + vars/default_vars.yml (mariadb_log_dir move); vars/local_vars_android_{small,medium,large}.yml + vars/local_vars_large.yml (forgejo section, install/enabled False)
Summary:         Add the Forgejo role (offline self-hosted Git forge) for K2GO-212. Serves at http://box/forgejo (nginx to 127.0.0.1:3300); sqlite by default; HTTP only under proot. Needs the K2GO-411 proot futex_time64 fix to run 32-bit on pre-5.1 kernels.

Mirrors upstream iiab/iiab#4505. This is the CONSOLIDATED net diff of the PR, not
its 13-commit mbox: the applier uses "patch -p1" with a reverse-dry-run
idempotency check, so a single net diff reverse-applies cleanly and is skipped
once #4505 ships in the pinned iiab commit. Text only, so it takes the "patch -p1"
path (no binary hunks). The role ships "forgejo_install/enabled: False" in every
vars file; K2Go's bake flips them True per tier in "iiab-android". Remove this
patch once #4505 merges into the pinned iiab commit.

